fix(recall): record a rescue that ran and found nothing (4.5.1)

4.5.0 logged only rescues that succeeded, which left two states indistinguishable in the audit:
recall-rewrite absent could mean the feature never ran, or that it ran and was useless. Four
releases (4.4.0-4.4.5) went to exactly that confusion, so the rule is applied here before it costs
anything.

Three events now: recall-rewrite when it found entries, recall-rewrite-empty when the model's
alternatives matched nothing, and recall-rewrite-skip with the reason when the route or reply was
unusable.

No behaviour change. The distinction is what makes tuning a question with data behind it: too many
recall-rewrite-empty rows would mean the hints or the alternative count need attention, rather than
leaving it to guesswork.
